Notebook[{Cell["AvNArgument", "ObjectName", ExpressionUUID -> "56f5e15f-4aac-4121-a079-c82a7772223b"], Cell["AvNArgument[scen, e] and AvNArgument[scen, e, d] give the All-vs-Nothing argument of the empirical model e on the scenario scen over Z_d (default d = 2; d is any integer >= 2, prime or composite), following Abramsky-Barbosa-Kishida-Lal-Mansfield, arXiv:1502.03097 Sec. 6: the theory of e collects every Z_d-affine equation Sum c_m x_m = a (mod d) satisfied by ALL support sections of a context; the model is AvN when the joint theory is inconsistent. Consistency is decided by an exact lattice-solvability test (Smith normal form of the integer coefficient matrix), valid over any Z_d and reducing to the GF(d) rank test when d is prime. For composite d the theory retains equations with NON-unit coefficient vectors (e.g. the 2x = 2 relations mod 4), which no prime-modulus reduction can see; equations are canonicalized only up to multiplication by units. AvN certifies strong contextuality, and every AvN model is cohomologically strongly contextual, so \"AvN\" -> True implies CechObstruction[scen, e][\"CohStronglyContextual\"]. Returns an association with keys \"Modulus\", \"Equations\" (as {context, coefficient tuple, rhs}), \"EquationCount\", \"Consistent\", and \"AvN\". GHZ is the canonical AvN model over Z_2 (the four Mermin parity equations); the Z_3 box on the square is AvN over Z_3; the Z_4 shift box is AvN over Z_4 with a witness invisible mod 2; the Hardy model is not AvN, matching its non-strong contextuality.", "Usage", ExpressionUUID -> "34567587-3902-4c5b-bc4f-1ea630a854f0"], Cell["Basic Examples", "Section", ExpressionUUID -> "b6d8995e-5acd-44af-b3a0-baf2ea23902a"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"AvNArgument", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"CycleScenario", "[", "5", "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", RowBox[{"5", ",", "\"Wright\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"AvN\"", "]"}]], "Input", ExpressionUUID -> "c0b4d286-41bc-46ec-af35-204d993525b0"]}, FrontEndVersion -> "15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)", StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb", ExpressionUUID -> "22034fd0-90e8-4993-bce0-d57b8ccec21b"]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
